Web source  : web/src/features/analytics/pages/FleetComparePage.tsx
Output      : apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/FleetComparePage/{FleetComparePage.Model.cs,
              FleetComparePage.Source.cs, FleetComparePage.ViewModel.cs, FleetComparePage.cs}
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client feed), <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view), exactly as the sibling W7
  CostAnalysisPage / OverviewVehicleComparison / BatteryComparison surfaces do. The generated prompt's idealized
  "FleetComparePage.xaml + FleetComparePageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Analytics" is mapped onto these real
  conventions; the surface registers itself with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("FleetCompare", already in
  RouteTable.cs L295 → /vehicle-comparison) via ShellWindow.xaml.cs, wiring NavigationRequested → NavigateTo.
- Data binding (ADR-004): the five manifest data sources (useVehicles GET /vehicles; useVehicleState
  GET /vehicles/{id}/state; useDrivingStats GET /drives/stats; useCostBreakdown GET /analytics/tco;
  useMonthlyMileage GET /mileage/monthly) are bound through one IFleetCompareSource. FleetCompareSource reads the
  roster (Operations.Vehicles.List) then fans out — concurrently per vehicle, exactly like BatteryComparison's
  Promise.all — the four per-vehicle reads (Operations.Vehicles.State path-scoped; Operations.Drives.Stats,
  Operations.Analytics.Tco, and the generated get_api_v1_mileage_monthly, each vehicle_id query-scoped). A failed
  per-vehicle slice is left null (web parity: the disabled/errored query → undefined). The assembled
  FleetCompareData is cached as JSON by the shared CacheThenNetworkEngine so it round-trips losslessly; the routes
  are confirmed in internal/api/router.go + the generated ApiEndpoints table. No HTTP touches the view. The
  parameterless page ctor uses EmptyFleetCompareSource (the established W7 default-feed pattern).
- Selection is a pure reprojection (web parity): the web roster + per-vehicle queries are already resolved and the
  two Selects just pick ids, so FleetComparePageViewModel auto-selects the first two vehicles (web useEffect),
  and SelectA/SelectB re-run FleetCompareProjection.Project over the already-loaded snapshot with NO refetch
  (asserted: ViewModel_select_reprojects_without_refetch keeps Attempts==1). Cross-disable (A≠B) is enforced both
  in the option lists (FleetCompareOption.Disabled) and the SelectA/SelectB guards.
- The web page renders states inside PageContainer per ADR-006, reproduced as visible Fluent regions: loading ->
  full-page skeleton (BuildLoadingSkeleton, TsGlassPanel/TsSkeleton shimmer); fewer-than-two vehicles -> the focused
  single-vehicle TsEmptyState with the Manage-vehicles CTA (web fleetCompare.singleVehicle.*); hard error -> the
  TsAlertBanner(Danger); success/stale/offline -> the content stack (selectors, side-by-side status cards, the two
  charts, the lifetime table, the highlights) with a TsDataFreshness chip. Each chart and each status card carries
  its OWN empty state (TsChartContainer ChartState.Empty for the no-data months; the select-vehicle status card) so
  no region is ever blank.
- SI at the display boundary (ADR-004/frontend-si-cutover): the source reads SI off the wire; FleetCompareProjection
  converts ONLY at projection time via the shared Core.Units converters/formatters (UnitConverters.DistanceFromSi /
  SpeedFromSi, UnitFormatters.FormatDistance / FormatTemperature / FormatEnergy, ScalarFormatters). The lifetime
  table reproduces the web fromKm / fromKmh / whPerKmToDisplay conversions and the getWinner semantics; the monthly
  distance chart restates the wire total_km to SI metres then converts to the user distance unit (the native
  MonthlyMileageWidget precedent, stricter than the web which left it km). rated_range is SI metres, inside/outside
  temp SI Celsius. Energy formats as kWh (web DEFAULT_ENERGY_PREF) via `units with { Energy = Kwh }`.
- i18n (ADR-014): every visible literal resolves through ILocalizer.GetString(key, web-default), web key names kept
  verbatim. All 43 declared comparison.* / fleetCompare.singleVehicle.* keys already exist in the auto-generated
  Strings/{en,he,ar}/Resources.resw (gen-i18n.ts output, do-not-hand-edit) — verified present (e.g. en L7083-L7200,
  L11262-L11270) — so no resw hand-edit was needed; the in-code English defaults match the web t() fallbacks.
- a11y (ADR-015): AutomationProperties names on the page, selectors, status cards and highlight cards; the charts
  publish AccessibleSummary (web ariaLabel) and expose the TsChartContainer data-table toggle; theme/light-dark flows
  from design tokens (DisplayTokens / StatusResources brushes) — no hardcoded hex. Colored/weighted text uses raw
  TextBlock (the typography controls render to an internal TextBlock and ignore Control.Foreground), matching the
  OverviewVehicleComparison precedent.

